nformation about health and healthy habits in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Relate information about health and healthy habits in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Relate information about health and healthy habits in social situations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le11ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Exploring Causes"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use these phrases to talk about or explore  the cause of something. You can also use <span class=\"strong\">modals</span>. Causes are the reasons why something happens.<span class=\"italic\"><br> <br>Thanks to \u2026 <br>It could be \u2026 <br>Are you sure it's ... ? <br>Could that be it? <br>It's possible it's ...</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Thanks to the sushi I ate."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's possible it's the sushi."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are you sure it's the chocolate?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "exhausted"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very tired"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am exhausted from shopping."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about an upset stomach."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "brutal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very bad"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a brutal stomach ache."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "notorious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "famous (usually for being bad)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Raw meat is notorious for making people sick."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dairy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "food made from cows' milk"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You don't eat dairy often, do you?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lie down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to  rest on a bed or couch"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should lie down and get some rest."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to check on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to monitor the state of someone (when they are sick) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to come and check on you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read each role below, and choose one."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice a conversation about the situation with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles and practice again."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Role 1: </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You are at home. You feel sick. You tell your mother or another family member. Talk about the causes of your stomach ache.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Role 2: </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You are at home. A family member feels sick. Talk about the causes of his/her stomach ache.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about health problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss causes of health problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice speaking in a conversation where someone is sick."}]}], "type": "sena"}